{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"747915178187817123","content":"Coney Island: large fairground at S of burrough. Entirely fairground/amusement park, including park areas\nSpitside: Ferrytown area of spit protruding from Hampstead. East side of the area is home to several ports used for both legitimate and illegitimate shipping, while the west section is one of the wilder feywild bleed-overs and a part of the Grassy Bay Bleed.\nGrassy Bay Bleed: The estuary-bay occupying the southeast coast of Ferrytown is home to large swaths of coastal feywild parks, many of which are islands. These parks are frequently used by smugglers to avoid watchful eyes, as it is exceedingly difficult to track a shipment that passes in and out of the feywild. The large swath near spitside is home to a large orchard.\nThe Bustle: A large market district in the center of Ferrytown that borders on and overlaps with several natural areas. If you want strange curios and other oddities, this is where you go. The shops are run by Seelie fey during the day and Unseelie fey during the night, meaning that different products may be available at different times.\nSunrise Port: Near the north end of Ferrytown and in full view of The City, the Sunrise Port is the main ferry port transporting between Ferrytown and The City, as well as up the channels to Kingsbridge.\nSunset Port: West of The Hilltops, the Sunset Port is the main ferry port transporting across the river from the Empire City.\nTwilight Port: Just north of Coney Island, the Twilight Port is the main ferry port transporting between Ferrytown and the Staten Wastes.","created_at":"2020-09-28T23:07:29.276000Z","edited_at":"2020-10-10T03:26:57.784000Z","id":"760276526935179304","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"747915178187817123","content":"The Hilltops: A stretch of hilly terrain near the center of Ferrytown, the East and West Hills are both places of feywild bleed over, though they are not connected. The most 'outsider friendly' of the feywild parks, they are adjacent to The Bustle and often full of younger teens and children, staying pleasantly warm for most of the day and year.\nThe Mounds: A major feywild park on the east edge of Ferrytown, the mostly flat but with small mounds of earth terrain of The Mounds makes it home to many fey who live under the small mounds. Its proximity to Hampstead and the associated gloom means it is a main dwelling place for Unseelie fey.\nRisehall: Stretching taller than most other buildings in Ferrytown, this area between the Sunrise and Sunset ports is home to visitors accustomed to more built-up dwellings. It also houses a population of mostly elf traders who commute to The City from Ferrytown each day. \nJameco: Named for the original human residents, Jameco is a community built primarily of these native peoples and fey bleed over. It is home to the Ferrytown court and resides between The Mounds and Grassy Bay.","created_at":"2020-09-28T23:07:31.214000Z","edited_at":null,"id":"760276535063085087","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
