{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"D (they/them)","id":"692746345387130900","is_bot":0,"username":"nonbianarydarry"},"author_id":"692746345387130900","channel_id":"747915178187817123","content":"Boats by clonetwins","created_at":"2020-10-10T05:16:08.032000Z","edited_at":"2020-10-10T05:16:22.387000Z","id":"764355566243545118","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"747915178187817123","content":"**Paddy's Pub**\nSituated on the south corner of the Western Hilltop park, this pub made of stone and wood is split down the middle and has two entrances: one on the feywild bleed side, and one that leads out into the more mundane section of The Bustle. There are no rules or firm divisions between the two sides, and mingling occurs frequently. Uncle Paddy is an older Kimellian man who speaks with a somewhat Irish accent. (Does this make sense? kinda, i guess?) Paddy is keen to offer advice to newcomers, as well as drinks and various potions. The drinks come in both alcoholic and non-alcoholic versions. One of the foods that is sold is a sugary grain cereal, marketed by someone who is in opposition to Kellog. To-go orders are allowed, but **all drinks bought at the pub will spoil the following dawn, becoming inert (albeit still alcoholic).**\nThe interior of the bar appears more slanted and uneven the more you approach the fey side, making it difficult not to spill your drink.","created_at":"2020-10-10T05:18:23.975000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-10T03:55:14.320000Z","id":"764356136429289482","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"747915178187817123","content":"**Items Available:**\nAirhead ale: This drink makes you feel light of both head and body. For the next hour, you levitate 5ft off of the ground at your walking speed, and descend at a rate of 5ft every 30ft if more than 5ft off of the ground. However, you find it hard to focus, and have disadvantage on saving throws to maintain concentration. 60gp.\nBegger's Bottle: This drink allows you to use the \"Grovel and Beg\" racial feature of Kobolds once in the next hour. 130gp.\nBanshee's Brew: This dark grey drink seems to wail mournfully at a low volume. When drunk, you can emit a mournful wail. ALL creatures within 30 feet of you must make a wisdom saving throw or take psychic damage equal to 2d8 plus your Charisma modifier. If you warn your allies ahead of time, they have advantage on this saving throw. 135gp.\nCizzle Cider: This drink container is home to a small fire elemental, and can either be drank to give you resistance to fire damage for the next ten minutes, or can be smashed against the ground, causing each creature within 10 feet of the item to make a DC 16 Dexterity saving throw or take 14 (4d6) fire damage. 250gp.\nThe Floral Ferment: This drink is sweet-smelling and enticing, giving you advantage on persuasion and deception checks for the next hour due to the sweet smell and charming demeanor it gives the drinker. 110gp.","created_at":"2020-10-10T05:24:21.083000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-10T02:27:12.809000Z","id":"764357634248933386","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
{"attachments":[],"author":{"display_name":"Eloise >:3c","id":"260820438026813440","is_bot":0,"username":"effervescenteloise"},"author_id":"260820438026813440","channel_id":"747915178187817123","content":"Grasping Guinness: When drank, this beverage makes your unarmed strikes have a reach of 15 feet and pull the target up to 10 feet closer to you on a successful hit as your arms elongate and become rubbery for the next hour. 185gp.\nLurching Leprechaun: This drink is constantly swirling and moving in the container. When drank, you gain the ability to take the *disengage* action as a bonus action as you sway around unpredictably. You also gain the ability to stand up from prone using only 5 feet of movement. These benefits last for 1 hour. 80 gp.\nTroublemaker's Tankard: When drank, this large tankard of popping ale gives you the ability to cast the *minor illusion* cantrip as a bonus action for the next hour. 150 gp.\nWine of Whimsy: This dark purple drink made from grapes causes the drinker to giggle for the next hour when not otherwise speaking, making them seem like less of a threat. Attacks against you have disadvantage if you have not damaged an enemy or used a negative effect on one this combat. 70 gp.","created_at":"2020-10-10T05:26:28.798000Z","edited_at":"2021-07-10T03:58:05.209000Z","id":"764358169924993065","reply_to_id":null,"thread":null,"thread_id":null}
